{
  "about": [
    "Client mode's contract between the app and arlesh-server, written as data (Task 9f0).",
    "",
    "`routes` maps every method of the app's Backend port (`src-tauri/src/backend/`) to the REST",
    "route(s) `HttpBackend` calls for it. `standalone_only` lists the methods with no route: People",
    "and the knowledge base, which HttpBackend refuses as not available in Client mode.",
    "`api_version` is the integer `/health` answers, bumped only on a breaking change.",
    "",
    "Both sides replay it. `src-tauri/src/backend/tests.rs` fails when a port method is in neither",
    "list, or a listed method is not on the port; `crates/arlesh-py/tests/server/integration/",
    "test_server_parity.py` fails when a listed route is not served or the server's `API_VERSION`",
    "differs. See `docs/spec/client-mode.md`, *REST parity*."
  ],
  "api_version": 1,
